`scan --cached` and `scan --rev` report a vaulted path in the index or in a commit, and match its bytes against the patterns, so a force-added vaulted file fails the pre-commit and pre-push hooks. Vaulted paths come from verified records and match by absolute path: an unsigned record no longer hides a file from the worktree walk, and a file in another repository that shares a stored relative name is not reported.
